.idea/

# Office lock files — created while a doc is open, never content
~$*

# Node
node_modules/
dist/

# Deck build artefacts and superseded decks — deliberately untracked.
# These are ~5MB of throwaway or superseded material, kept locally so the
# renders can be regenerated, but not worth carrying in the repository:
#   _render_check/  crop scripts + raw diagram PNGs used to build slide images
#   canvas/         the older canvas HTML deck, superseded by poc-canvas/
#   Granite.pptx    a 10-slide deck separate from both tracked decks
# The tracked decks are Granite_Proposal_Defense.pptx (v1) and
# Granite_Proposal_Defense_v2.pptx (v2, current).
markdowns/05-deliverables/proposal-deck/_render_check/
markdowns/05-deliverables/proposal-deck/canvas/
markdowns/05-deliverables/proposal-deck/Granite.pptx

# Notes
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# dev/datasets/ is currently TRACKED in this repository (~46MB of
# third-party datasets and one fully vendored upstream repo).
#
# That is a deliberate, temporary state, not an oversight. Before this
# repository is made public, read dev/datasets/DOWNLOAD.md — it records
# each dataset's source, license and retrieval command, and flags GAIA,
# whose gated access terms make redistribution a licensing problem.
#
# When the team acts on that, uncomment the line below and replace the
# tracked directory with DOWNLOAD.md's retrieval scripts:
#
# dev/datasets/
#
# Do NOT ignore dev/spikes/poc/*.json — those output files are
# proposal-defense evidence (guide §12) and belong in git.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
